# Failed Fording with its target gone (CR 608.2b): Bot1 controls a Desert (Shefet Dunes) and casts Failed Fording at Bot2's
# Ornithopter, then in response Bot1's own Lightning Bolt kills the Ornithopter. The spell resolves with no legal target, does
# nothing at all, and so does not surveil even though Bot1 controls a Desert: the Ornithopter is in Bot2's graveyard (not in its
# hand) and the Forest on top is drawn at turn 5.

[Bot1 Deck]
Shefet Dunes
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Island
Failed Fording
Lightning Bolt
Island
Mountain
Forest
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Plains x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Shefet Dunes.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Failed Fording.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Arrange
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand = Forest; Island; Mountain

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Plains; Ornithopter
Bot1.Graveyard = Failed Fording; Lightning Bolt
Stack.Count = 0
